# ─── AgentShield Environment Variables ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# Pick ONE of the free API providers below.
# GitHub Models is preferred (Microsoft ecosystem, free with GitHub account).
#
# Option 1: GitHub Models, recommended and free through Microsoft Azure Foundry
# Get your token: https://github.com/settings/tokens → Generate new token (classic) → no scopes needed
# NOTE: leave this commented until you have a real token. An uncommented placeholder
# value makes every request try (and fail) an 8-second LLM call before falling back.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_personal_access_token_here

# ── Option 2: Groq (free tier, very fast, Llama 3.1) ─────────────────────────
# Get your key: https://console.groq.com/
# GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here

# ── Option 3: OpenRouter (free models available) ──────────────────────────────
# Get your key: https://openrouter.ai/
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here

# ── Note: Pattern-only mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If no API key is set, AgentShield still works using its 60+ pattern database.
# LLM deep analysis will be skipped but detection remains highly effective.

# ── Synthetic / demo data (both default OFF) ──────────────────────────────────
# By default a fresh deploy shows nothing but real inspected traffic - no fake
# history, no background noise. Turn these on only for a showcase/demo:
# AGENTSHIELD_SEED_DATA=true       # backfill 7 fake days of history on first boot
# AGENTSHIELD_DEMO_TRAFFIC=true    # emit a fabricated event every 10-15s forever
# Any event either of these produces is tagged session_id="demo_..." and
# source="demo" everywhere it's stored or broadcast, and the dashboard/pipeline
# UI visibly badges it "SYNTHETIC" - it is never presented as real traffic.

# ── Retention ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AGENTSHIELD_EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# AGENTSHIELD_EVENT_CLEANUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=3600
